subproblem.statement:
Let P, m ∈ ℕ, n := m + 1, I : Fin n → Fin P strictly increasing, θ an n-covector on ℝ^P with θ(v) = det(v_j(I k))_{k,j} for all v (θ = dx^I), and b : ℝ^P → ℝ C^∞ with compact support. Then there is K ∈ ℝ such that the following holds for every C^∞ map g : ℝⁿ → ℝⁿ with ‖g(y)‖ ≤ 1 for all y. There are C^∞ compactly supported forms η of degree m and ζ of degree n on ℝ^P (IsTestForm) such that:
- tsupport η ⊆ tsupport b and tsupport ζ ⊆ tsupport b;
- covectorEuclideanNorm(η(x)) ≤ K and covectorEuclideanNorm(ζ(x)) ≤ K for all x;
- dη(x) = (b(x)·div g(p_I x))•θ + ζ(x) for all x (exteriorDerivative).
Here p_I(x) := WithLp.toLp 2 (fun k => x (I k)) ∈ ℝⁿ, and div g(y) is the trace of Dg(y).

Let P, n, d ∈ ℕ, U ⊆ ℝ^P open, and T ∈ 𝒟_n(U) (GeometricCurrentOn U n) with M_W(T) < ∞ for every open W ⊂⊂ U (CompactlyContained W U: closure W is compact and contained in U). Let c : Λⁿ(ℝ^P) → ℝ^d (Covector (Euclid P) n ≃L[ℝ] EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d)) be a continuous linear equivalence with covectorEuclideanNorm α = ‖c α‖ for all α. Then there is a real linear functional L on C_c(U, ℝ^d) (CompactlySupportedContinuousMap ↥U (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d)), U with the subspace topology) such that:
(i) L(g) = T(ω) whenever ω ∈ 𝒟ⁿ(U), g ∈ C_c(U, ℝ^d) and g(x) = c(ω(x)) for all x ∈ U;
(ii) for every compact K ⊆ U (a compact subset of the subtype) there is M ∈ ℝ with |L(g)| ≤ M for every g ∈ C_c(U, ℝ^d) with tsupport g ⊆ K and ‖g(x)‖ ≤ 1 for all x.

Let P, n ∈ ℕ, U ⊆ ℝ^P open, and T ∈ 𝒟_n(U) with M_W(∂T) < ∞ for every open W ⊂⊂ U (boundaryMassOn, read as 0 when n = 0). Let μ be a Borel measure on ℝ^P and ξ : ℝ^P → Λ_n a map into the n-vectors (MultiVector P n) such that:
- μ(ℝ^P ∖ U) = 0;
- μ(K) < ∞ for every compact K ⊆ U;
- M_W(T) = μ(W) for every open W;
- ξ is μ-a.e. strongly measurable;
- |ξ(x)(α)| ≤ covectorEuclideanNorm α for all x and α;
- T(ω) = ∫ ξ(x)(ω(x)) dμ(x) for all ω ∈ 𝒟ⁿ(U).
Then μ(E) = 0 for every E ⊆ ℝ^P with μHE[n](E) = 0.

Let P, n ∈ ℕ, U ⊆ ℝ^P open, and T ∈ 𝒟_n(U) (GeometricCurrentOn U n) with M_W(T) = T.massOn W < ∞ for every open W ⊂⊂ U (CompactlyContained W U: closure W is compact and contained in U). Then there are a Borel measure μ on ℝ^P and a map ξ : ℝ^P → Λ_n into the n-vectors (MultiVector P n, the continuous linear functionals on n-covectors) such that:
- μ(ℝ^P ∖ U) = 0;
- μ(K) < ∞ for every compact K ⊆ U;
- M_W(T) = μ(W) for every open W ⊆ ℝ^P;
- ξ is μ-a.e. strongly measurable;
- |ξ(x)(α)| ≤ covectorEuclideanNorm α for every x and every n-covector α;
- T(ω) = ∫ ξ(x)(ω(x)) dμ(x) for every ω ∈ 𝒟ⁿ(U).
